Comment: /usr/bin/jkit is compiled ahead of time with GraalVM Native Image. It
 contains jkit's own code and the Java libraries below, compiled in; the
 stanzas after "Files: *" name each library by its Maven coordinates rather
 than by a path in this package. /usr/share/doc/jkit/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES holds
 their NOTICE files verbatim. The binary also contains parts of the GraalVM
 Community Edition and OpenJDK runtime, licensed GPL-2 with the Classpath
 Exception, and the third-party code the OpenJDK class library carries (Xerces,
 Xalan, ICU, Unicode CLDR data, zlib and others): THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES has their
 notices under "Java runtime", the full license text, and where to get the source.

